{
  "manufacturer": "HindlePower",
  "manufacturer_slug": "hindlepower",
  "model": "ATevo battery charger (Modbus communications adapter)",
  "model_slug": "atevo",
  "short_model": "ATevo",
  "aliases": [
    "ATevo",
    "ATevo Communications"
  ],
  "equipment_type": "Battery charger (industrial float charger, UPS-type DC system)",
  "applies_to": "HindlePower ATevo battery chargers with the serial or Ethernet communications adapter set to Modbus, per the ATevo Communications online manual version 1.3.",
  "summary": "HindlePower's ATevo industrial battery charger supports Modbus RTU on its serial communications adapter and Modbus TCP on the Ethernet adapter. Charger options are coils, about 60 alarm and status flags are discrete inputs, measurements (DC and AC voltages and currents, ground-fault data) are input registers and all setpoints are holding registers, with fixed multipliers. This map covers the published Modbus register set apart from a few values whose sign or units are not stated.",
  "transport": [
    "RTU",
    "TCP"
  ],
  "defaults": {
    "unit_id": null,
    "baud": null,
    "parity": null,
    "data_bits": null,
    "stop_bits": null,
    "tcp_port": 502
  },
  "addressing": {
    "convention": "Modicon",
    "note": "Tables use Modicon references (00001 coils, 10001 discrete inputs, 30001 input registers, 40001 holding registers) and the implementation follows the Modicon PI-MBUS-300 guide, so 30001 is input register 0 on the wire and 40001 holding register 0."
  },
  "default_word_order": "CDAB",
  "firmware": null,
  "source": {
    "title": "ATevo Communications (online manual) - Modbus sections 6.1-6.6",
    "doc_number": "Version 1.3",
    "revision_date": "2026-08-28",
    "url": "https://www.manula.com/manuals/hindlepower-inc/atevo-communications/1.3/en/topic/modbus-holding-registers",
    "pages": "Sections 6.1 (introduction), 6.2 (function codes), 6.3 (coils), 6.4 (binary inputs), 6.5 (input registers, https://www.manula.com/manuals/hindlepower-inc/atevo-communications/1.3/en/topic/modbus-input-registers), 6.6 (holding registers); 4.1.3 and 4.2.4 (address and TCP port)"
  },
  "notes": [
    "This is HindlePower's own manual, published on the manula.com documentation platform (each section is a separate page).",
    "Scaling: divide the raw value by the Multiplier column (10 for XXX.X values, 100 for XXX.XX). Scale = 1 / multiplier.",
    "32-bit timestamps are split into a 'Low' and a 'High' register with the low word in the lower address (CDAB): 30018/30019 battery open test time and 40022/40023 date/time, both seconds since 1 January 2000.",
    "Left out: 30002 Modbus firmware revision (format 'XXX.xxx.0' cannot be decoded from one register), 30009 (not used), 30010 battery temperature, 30011 rectifier temperature, 30020 ambient temperature, 30029/30030 battery current (the manual does not say whether negative values are sent as signed integers).",
    "30013/30014 (positive/negative terminal to ground) are listed without units because the manual gives none.",
    "Some entries are only reported when the matching optional hardware is installed (e.g. AC meter option for 30022-30028).",
    "Valid ranges of many setpoints depend on the charger rating; see HindlePower supplement JA5124-02. Writing outside the range returns an exception."
  ],
